' F9 -- Core physical schema, part 1: identity, Spaces and content, parsing.
' Chapter 4 (Design). ER diagram, crow's-foot ends carry the multiplicities.
' Claim supported: of 79 tables in supabase/migrations/ at dfc20df6 (distinct CREATE
' TABLE names, one of them learning_events_default, the event table's default
' partition; 78 without it), 36 (plus
' auth.users) constitute the domain; 19 are drawn here, 17 in F9b. A Space has
' no table of its own; one relationship here carries NO database-enforced FK.
' Split from F9b because 37 boxes cannot print legibly on one A4 page.
@startuml f9-er-core
!include _style.iuml

title Core schema, part 1: identity, Spaces, content, parsing

hide methods
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 10
skinparam ranksep 14
left to right direction

  class "auth.users" as auth_users <<supabase>> {
    +id
  }
  class profiles {
    user_id FK
    total_xp, current_streak
    show_in_spaces
    luna_loadout : jsonb
  }
  class user_roles {
    user_id FK
    role : app_role
  }
  class onboarding_progress {
    +user_id FK
  }

  class courses {
    +id
    professor_id FK
    status : draft / published
  }
  class course_context {
    +course_id FK
  }
  class lectures {
    +id
    course_id FK //nullable//
    professor_id FK //nullable//
    student_owner_id FK
    visibility, pdf_hash
  }
  class slides {
    +id
    lecture_id FK
    slide_number, summary
  }
  class quiz_questions {
    +id
    slide_id FK
    correct_answer
  }
  class worksheets {
    lecture_id FK
  }
  class lecture_pages {
    +lecture_id FK, +page : int
    blocks, summary : jsonb
  }

  class course_enrollments {
    user_id FK
    course_id FK
  }
  class assignments {
    professor_id FK
    course_id //no FK//
  }
  class assignment_lectures {
    assignment_id, lecture_id
  }
  class assignment_enrollments {
    assignment_id, user_id
  }

  class parse_runs {
    +run_id
    lecture_id FK
    user_id, pdf_hash, status
  }
  class parse_receipts {
    +run_id FK
    lecture_id FK
  }
  class slide_embeddings {
    lecture_id FK
    {field} embedding : vector(768)
  }

  class concepts {
    +id
    name_key : text UNIQUE
  }
  class concept_lectures {
    concept_id, lecture_id
    slide_indices : int[]
  }

auth_users ||--|| profiles
auth_users ||--o{ user_roles
auth_users ||--o| onboarding_progress
auth_users ||--o{ course_enrollments
courses ||--o{ course_enrollments
courses ||--o| course_context
courses |o--o{ lectures
lectures ||--o{ slides
slides ||--o{ quiz_questions
worksheets }o--|| lectures
lecture_pages }o--|| lectures
lectures |o--o{ parse_runs
parse_runs ||--o| parse_receipts
lectures |o--o{ slide_embeddings
lectures ||--o{ concept_lectures
concepts ||--o{ concept_lectures
assignments ||--o{ assignment_lectures
lectures ||--o{ assignment_lectures
assignments ||--o{ assignment_enrollments

' --- Unenforced relationship: DASHED, no FK in the database ---
courses .. assignments

note bottom of courses
  **No spaces table.** A Space is a
  courses row; joining adds a
  course_enrollments row. The personal
  Space's id is its owner's user id.
end note

legend bottom
  Ids and FKs are uuid unless typed. Dashed = no database-enforced foreign key.
  Every other user / owner / professor column also references auth.users
  (edges omitted). Part 2 (next figure): learning, Luna, gamification.
endlegend

@enduml
